    {
      "source": "If you write a <code>Converter</code> whose source and target type are native types, we cannot determine whether we should consider it as a reading or a writing converter.\nRegistering the converter instance as both might lead to unwanted results.\nFor example, a <code>Converter&lt;String, Long&gt;</code> is ambiguous, although it probably does not make sense to try to convert all <code>String</code> instances into <code>Long</code> instances when writing.\nTo let you force the infrastructure to register a converter for only one way, we provide <code>@ReadingConverter</code> and <code>@WritingConverter</code> annotations to be used in the converter implementation.",
      "translation": "如果您编写了一个源类型和目标类型均为原生类型的<code>Converter</code>，我们无法确定应将其视为读取转换器还是写入转换器。  \n将转换器实例同时注册为两者可能会导致意外结果。  \n例如，<code>Converter&lt;String, Long&gt;</code>具有歧义性，尽管在写入时尝试将所有<code>String</code>实例转换为<code>Long</code>实例可能并不合理。  \n为了让您强制基础设施只为单一方向注册转换器，我们提供了<code>@ReadingConverter</code>和<code>@WritingConverter</code>注解，可在转换器实现中使用。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "The following example of a Spring <code>Converter</code> implementation converts from a <code>String</code> to a custom <code>Email</code> value object:",
      "translation": "以下是一个 Spring <code>Converter</code> 实现的示例，它用于将 <code>String</code> 转换为自定义的 <code>Email</code> 值对象：",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "JSR-310 Converters for conversion between <code>java.time</code>, <code>java.util.Date</code> and <code>String</code> types.",
      "translation": "用于在 `<code>java.time</code>`、`<code>java.util.Date</code>` 和 `<code>String</code>` 类型之间进行转换的 JSR-310 转换器。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Generally, we inspect the <code>Converter</code> implementations for the source and target types they convert from and to.\nDepending on whether one of those is a type the underlying data access API can handle natively, we register the converter instance as a reading or a writing converter.\nThe following examples show a writing-  and a read converter (note the difference is in the order of the qualifiers on <code>Converter</code>):",
      "translation": "通常，我们会检查 `<code>Converter`</code> 实现所转换的源类型和目标类型。根据这些类型中是否有一种是底层数据访问 API 能够原生处理的，我们将转换器实例注册为读取转换器或写入转换器。以下示例展示了一个写入转换器和一个读取转换器（请注意 `<code>Converter`</code> 上限定词顺序的差异）：",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "Converters are subject to explicit registration as instances are not picked up from a classpath or container scan to avoid unwanted registration with a conversion service and the side effects resulting from such a registration. Converters are registered with <code>CustomConversions</code> as the central facility that allows registration and querying for registered converters based on source- and target type.",
      "translation": "转换器必须进行显式注册，因为实例不会被从类路径或容器扫描中自动拾取，以避免与转换服务发生不需要的注册以及由此产生的副作用。转换器通过 <code>CustomConversions</code> 进行注册，该组件是中央设施，允许基于源类型和目标类型注册和查询已注册的转换器。",
      "count": 1
    },
    {
      "source": "<code>CustomConversions</code> ships with a pre-defined set of converter registrations:",
      "translation": "<code>CustomConversions</code> 附带一组预定义的转换器注册：",
      "count": 1
    },
